# The machines themselves, one directory per architecture: a twenty gigabyte
# disk with a saved state inside it, the firmware's writable half, the seed it
# first booted from, and the key that reaches it.
#
# None of it is source and all of it is made by `build.sh` — which is what is
# tracked, so anybody can make their own.
aarch64/
x86_64/

# And the images Ubuntu publishes, kept so that building a machine again is a
# conversion rather than a download.
cache/
